# Repo-root .vercelignore — used when `vercel deploy` runs from the repo
# root (required for a monorepo project with a "Root Directory" setting:
# Vercel needs the whole tree uploaded so it can scope into that
# subdirectory server-side; deploying directly from inside the
# subdirectory double-nests the path and fails). CLI deploy uploads the
# raw filesystem regardless of .gitignore, so this needs its own excludes.
node_modules/
dist/
apps/api/data/
.git/
*.log
# Loose local-only files sitting at the repo root (never committed,
# nothing to do with the app) — root-anchored so this doesn't also catch
# real build assets like apps/web/public/*.png.
/*.MOV
/*.mov
/*.jpeg
/*.jpg
/*.png
